If you grind monsters indefinitely, the monsters will all be different.
Some won't respect Elbereth. Some will rust or disenchant your weapon.
Some will summon other monsters. If you grind puddings, all you get is
puddings, puddings, puddings. They're scriptable. You can't just script
casting create monster and killing the results. Imagine reading "You
hear the cockatrice's hissing!" in the middle of 10000 lines of output...

Certainly you can grind monsters with effort and time, but I think
pudding farming's effort to results ratio is much lower. It doesn't
bother me as much as it bothers some people, but I don't think it would
do the game a disservice to take it away.

